<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lakota people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Teton Sioux</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lakota, or Teton Sioux, are the westernmost division of the Oceti Sakowin, made up of seven bands including the Oglala, Hunkpapa, Sicangu and Miniconjou. Moving west from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minnesota">Minnesota</a> in the 18th century, they became mounted bison hunters and the leading power of the northern Plains, reaching the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-hills">Black Hills</a> by around 1776. Leaders such as Red Cloud, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sitting-bull">Sitting Bull</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crazy-horse">Crazy Horse</a> resisted US expansion until the late 1870s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lakota-people.jpg" alt="Lakota people" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Francis Barry · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En-chief-sitting-bull.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
